James asked for C++ code to add a new loader for NetCDF files into his `GeographicMap` class, which processes geographic data. I provided a strict 2-D loader, ensuring that variable dimensions are ordered as `[latitude, longitude]`. After learning that the target variable included a time dimension with a single entry, he requested to generalize the loader to accommodate dimensions `[latitude, longitude]` or `[time, latitude, longitude]`. I modified the loader to check for both cases, verifying that if time exists, it has length one and that the lat/lon dimensions match the input ranges. The provided solution maintains the population of values in the matrix from the buffer consistently, ensuring compatibility with both dimension specifications.
